# GUI verification

Apply this section when changing or verifying Swing, input, menus, Diff, notifications or other GUI behavior. The always-on [shared rule](loop-engineering.mdc) retains ownership/integration/safety requirements for every task; documentation-only work does not trigger GUI testing.

- Use `docs/verification/changes/issue-N.json` and fixed-candidate result JSON as authority under [verification](../../docs/verification/README.md). Old manual-verification matrices/runs are history; `current.md` is generated.
- Add/update affected Cases, steps, expectations and evidence. Keep human-facing steps/expectations in Japanese under the [context policy](../../docs/architecture/knowledge.md#開発コンテキストの用途言語形式と読込条件).
- A designated, capable and authorized operator observes the real screen under the GUI lease; a human may take an explicit handoff. Preserve Computer Use-required Cases. An agent’s own reply is not evidence of GUI success.
- Record target SHA, loaded build, steps, expected/actual result, evidence, observer and date.
- Keep `pending / pass / fail / blocked`; retrieval failures are blocked. Merge alone does not complete/archive verification.
- Recheck fixes in a new run. CLI/JUnit success is not a GUI pass. Follow finish-work for develop/main gates and QA transfer; do not duplicate results here.
